==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Normalization}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|normalisation}} ''UK''

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|normal|ization}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Any process that makes something more [[normal]] or [[regular]], which typically means conforming to some regularity or rule, or returning from some state of abnormality.
# [[standardization]], act of imposing [[standard]]s or [[norm]]s or [[rule]]s or [[regulation]]s.
# {{lb|en|databases}} In [[relational database]] [[design]], a [[process]] that breaks down [[data]] into [[record]] [[group]]s for [[efficient]] [[processing]], by [[eliminating]] [[redundancy]].
# {{lb|en|diplomacy}} Process of establishing normal diplomatic relations between two countries
# {{lb|en|economics}} [[globalization]], the process of making a worldwide [[normal]] and dominant model of [[production]] and [[consumption]]
# {{lb|en|operations}} Making a [[normalized production]].
# {{lb|en|politics}} Sharing or enforcement of [[standard policies]]
# {{lb|en|sociology}} A process whereby artificial and unwanted [[norms of behaviour]] and [[model]]s of [[behaviour]] are made to seem [[natural]] and [[wanted]], through [[propaganda]], [[influence]], [[imitation]] and [[conformity]].
# {{lb|en|statistics}} The process of removing statistical error in repeated measured data.

